  "answer": "You can add middleware to a FastAPI application by using the `@app.middleware(\"http\")` decorator on top of a function. The middleware function receives the `request` and a function `call_next` that will receive the `request` as a parameter. You can then further modify the `response` before returning it.\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi.middleware import Middleware\nfrom fastapi import Request\n\n@app.middleware(\"http\")\nasync def middleware_function(request: Request, call_next):\n    # Your middleware code here\n    response = await call_next(request)\n    # Modify the response here\n    return response\n```\n\n[reference/middleware-0]",
